{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion","id":151543,"title":"Science in Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-28T11:52:17-07:00","id":151543,"title":"Science in Scion","content":"I noticed this from the Discovery News YouTube channel:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So apparently, lightning is caused by the Sun. Would this mean that the Boons from the Sky purview pertaining to Lightning attacks would actually be part of the Sun purview, or are the purviews too mythical for science (in the same way that conservatives are too political for facts)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:10:01-07:00","id":151573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion#post151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed this from the Discovery News YouTube channel:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So apparently, lightning is caused by the Sun. Would this mean that the Boons from the Sky purview pertaining to Lightning attacks would actually be part of the Sun purview, or are the purviews too mythical for science (in the same way that conservatives are too political for facts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Purviews are incredibly mythical, and this is a case of Science Marching On; I would not allow Sun to control lightning, because lightning comes during the thunder storms and the rain and to the ancient cultures, that was the connection and correlation. Even the Sun Purview itself is not really that science-y (or it won't be once we get our hands on it).<br /> <br /> We want, for Scion 2.0, for the purviews to remain mythically viable but capable of being used for modern-day concepts. If someone wanted to connect the Sun and Lightning, they could simply take the Sky/Thunder purview along with sun and combine them in a awesome way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:24:00-07:00","id":151583,"title":"","content":"Modern Science is amazing, and awesome, but very much has problems with Scion. The Ancient peoples related concepts that may have no relations between them in reality, but since we are playing a game centered around their religious beliefs, we have to go with them.<br /> <br /> For example, the concept of the Fertility of the land, represented through the Fertility Purview, was often also conflated with large genitals in Gods, and your standard Fertility Goddess figure. Even though we know that there is no relation between the fertility of all corn in the universe, and the capability for to people to have children, the Gods and Goddesses of Fertility in Scion are likely incredibly sexual beings who have almost nega-birth control.<br /> <br /> Additionally, you get things like the issues with the brain. If a ST runs that Ichor overcomes flesh, a Theoi Scion could walk around without a brain in his head but be entirely functional except that his bloodboils (good Fire Relic, that), though then you get into competing ideas between cultures, since if an Irish Scion didn't have a brain, they would be dead a thousand times over for they conflated the soul and the brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:25:44-07:00","id":151584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion#post151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently, lightning is caused by the Sun. Would this mean that the Boons from the Sky purview pertaining to Lightning attacks would actually be part of the Sun purview, or are the purviews too mythical for science (in the same way that conservatives are too political for facts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion really does follow the Law of Myth and not the Law of Science. Purviews represent those ancient beliefs about the world being true, so none of them should fundamentally be about modern science as we know it. But that does not stop an enterprising Scion from using those ancient Purviews to accomplish modern scientific things!<br /> <br /> Stunting even allows you to depict the consequences of those Purviews in a scientific fashion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:18:59-07:00","id":151622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion#post151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed this from the Discovery News YouTube channel:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqI2T2f5mnE&amp;index=25&amp;list=UUzWQYUVCpZqtN93H8RR44Qw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So apparently, lightning is caused by the Sun. Would this mean that the Boons from the Sky purview pertaining to Lightning attacks would actually be part of the Sun purview, or are the purviews too mythical for science (in the same way that conservatives are too political for facts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fact that a scion has the potential to live 10 ton should answer all questions of Myth vs Science","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T16:49:55-07:00","id":151821,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and 10 tons is for those light weights. The heavyweights are tossing battleships to the moon when they aren't biting anvils in half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:13:34-07:00","id":152084,"title":"","content":"This is actually interesting, since a number of Amazonian tribes did believe that lightning was sent by the sun... <br /> <br /> Specifically, that it was the Sun's semen. <br /> <br /> The Amazon is a weird place mythologically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:36:34-07:00","id":152094,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of this:<br /> <i><br /> <u>Holy Shit! It\u2019s gold!</u><br /> The Incas apparently believed that gold and silver<br /> were literally the feces of the gods.<br /> --Dead Magic Black Dog Game Factory (by Dana Habecker, Jess Heinig, James Stewart and Chris Tang)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:20:13-07:00","id":152143,"title":"","content":"Technically, THAT was the Aztecs. Their word for gold literally translated to &quot;god-shit&quot;. Silver was &quot;white god-shit&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, take a look at a lump of unworked gold and tell me you don't see the similarities...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T05:15:21-07:00","id":152375,"title":"","content":"I was just quoting for the sake of amusement...(and I don't have the time to dig in their bibliography)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:44:25-07:00","id":160791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion?p=152084#post152084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Amazon is a weird place mythologically</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the aztecs with their bloody babies suckling on trees with nipples beat that. Or the time Horus tricked Set into eating his semen so he could prove to Osiris who the bitch in the relationship was...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T13:39:53-07:00","id":161045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion?p=160791#post160791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the aztecs with their bloody babies suckling on trees with nipples beat that. Or the time Horus tricked Set into eating his semen so he could prove to Osiris who the bitch in the relationship was...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Amazon has a monster-god called the Kurupi. He's a stunted, hairy, ugly, ugly dwarf who is the embodiment of rape. He has a penis that is so long that when not in use he wears it as a belt, coiled several times around his torso. He can maneuver it through the cracks between the walls to get at a girl and knock her up. Or, if he's in a hurry that day, he can impregnate her with a mere touch. <br /> <br /> And we're only on the tip of the iceberg here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T15:00:00-07:00","id":161159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion?p=161045#post161045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Amazon has a monster-god called the Kurupi. He's a stunted, hairy, ugly, ugly dwarf who is the embodiment of rape. He has a penis that is so long that when not in use he wears it as a belt, coiled several times around his torso. He can maneuver it through the cracks between the walls to get at a girl and knock her up. Or, if he's in a hurry that day, he can impregnate her with a mere touch.<br /> <br /> And we're only on the tip of the iceberg here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not even that strange. Barnacles have penises roughly 40 times their body length.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:07:29-07:00","id":161236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we're only on the tip of the iceberg here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't you mean the tip of the pe...o never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:05:24-07:00","id":195186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/151543-science-in-scion#post151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently, lightning is caused by the Sun. Would this mean that the Boons from the Sky purview pertaining to Lightning attacks would actually be part of the Sun purview, or are the purviews too mythical for science (in the same way that conservatives are too political for facts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it on one condition, if the scion that wants to use it is a scion of Science. Ever read American Gods from Neil Gaiman? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> He had a pretty good idea about modern gods, like Media, Internet, the Intangibles (the Invisible Hand of the market), etc. We, the people tend to believe in things which come from the Media, is on one of the countless websites, etc. These things really exist, but they are also the foci of belief, so in some way or another they could be considered deities. Looking at this from this point of view, Science could also be considered a focus of belief, and its followers are the scientists, who work in the field. A player could play a scion, who is one of the numerous children of Science, or going back to the more traditional gods, a scion of Minerva/Athene/Cydonia/Saraswati/Seshat or if gender matters from the male side Oghma/Djehuty/Ganesha/Enki/Quetzalcoatl (sorry for not mentioning Far Eastern examples, I'm not that into them). These examples are from cultures which possessed the knowledge of science in their peak of existance, that knowledge they practiced are still considered science. Religion and science walked hands in hands with each other even before the age of enlightenment, only Christianity had its debates with science during the Middle Ages. So a scion of Science could I think derive its powers from a different source than other scions, (s)he'd get a limit though to these powers, 'cause this though pattern is still incorporated into the reality of the more traditional perspective of the game, not the other way around, but one shouldn't discard an unorthodox idea without a proper explanation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2554-sol","name":"Sol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}